{
  "title": "The Entangled Blade",
  "bpm": 120,
  "sampleRate": 48000,
  "duration": 200,
  "voices": {
    "narrator": {
      "model": "en-us-ryan-high",
      "lengthScale": 1.08
    },
    "alien": {
      "model": "en-gb-alan-low",
      "lengthScale": 1.15,
      "alien": true
    }
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 1.5,
      "text": "Space is silent. With no air to carry it, even a scream dies at the lips."
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 11.0,
      "text": "Past the Moon, where the pull of Earth and the pull of the Moon balance out, a single keeper tends the relay."
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 18.5,
      "text": "On day four hundred, a ship came falling inward, at eight tenths of the speed of light."
    },
    {
      "id": "n4",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 24.5,
      "text": "At that speed, space itself shortens along the line of motion. The ship arrives squeezed to three fifths of its length, and its light is pushed toward blue."
    },
    {
      "id": "n5",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 35.0,
      "text": "Its clocks run slow. While the keeper waited five years, the traveler aged three."
    },
    {
      "id": "n6",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 41.0,
      "text": "And light takes time to travel. The ship he saw was already a memory. By the time its image arrived, the traveler was here."
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "voice": "alien",
      "at": 51.5,
      "text": "Keeper. You hold the other half of my blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "n7",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 57.0,
      "text": "Two blades, forged as an entangled pair. Two halves of a single quantum state."
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "voice": "alien",
      "at": 62.5,
      "text": "Return it. Or fight for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "n8",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 66.5,
      "text": "One more thing. What you are about to hear is not sound crossing space. It is vibration, carried through steel, glove, and bone."
    },
    {
      "id": "n9",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 87.0,
      "text": "Every push is shared. When the blades meet, both fighters fly apart, equal and opposite. Momentum is conserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "n10",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 100.5,
      "text": "The keeper pulls his limbs in. Same angular momentum, smaller body. He spins faster."
    },
    {
      "id": "n11",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 114.0,
      "text": "The alien's blade is not in one place. It is a cloud of maybes, until something touches it."
    },
    {
      "id": "n12",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 131.0,
      "text": "He raises a barrier. Most of the wave reflects. But a quantum wave never fully stops. A sliver tunnels through."
    },
    {
      "id": "n13",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 158.0,
      "text": "Then the keeper measures his own blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "n14",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 161.5,
      "text": "Spin up. And across the gap, with nothing crossing it, the other blade is spin down."
    },
    {
      "id": "n15",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 171.5,
      "text": "No signal outran light. The answer was shared from the start. Entanglement carries no message. Only agreement."
    },
    {
      "id": "n16",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 180.5,
      "text": "The traveler left, its light sliding into red. Three years home, by its own clock. Five, by ours."
    },
    {
      "id": "n17",
      "voice": "narrator",
      "at": 189.0,
      "text": "And the lost blade drifts on, in a straight line, forever. Nothing out here will ever stop it."
    }
  ],
